.TH QUARTEREXAMINERVIEWER 3 "2026-10-22" "QuarterExaminerViewer" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
QuarterExaminerViewer \- An SoQtExaminerViewer\-style viewer for Coin3D, built on Quarter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqQuarterExaminerViewer.h\(dq
.sp
.B class QuarterExaminerViewer : public QWidget
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBQuarterExaminerViewer\fR is a Qt widget that gives applications
built on the Quarter library the look, feel and functionality of the
classic \fBSoQtExaminerViewer\fR. Quarter supplies the OpenGL canvas;
\fBQuarterExaminerViewer\fR adds the viewer decoration (buttons and
thumbwheels), mouse navigation, a popup menu, a preferences dialog, an
animated seek function, a home position and perspective/orthographic
camera switching.
.PP
The class derives from \fBQWidget\fR, so it can be used as a top\-level
window or embedded in any layout. The underlying \fBQuarterWidget\fR is
available through \fBquarterWidget()\fR for anything the class does not
wrap.
.SS Defaults
.IP \(bu 3
Starts in View mode (the mouse navigates the camera).
.IP \(bu 3
Headlight on; black background; decoration visible.
.IP \(bu 3
Seek: 2.0 seconds, 50 % of the current distance, seeks to the picked
point.
.IP \(bu 3
Right\-click popup menu enabled.
.IP \(bu 3
Default window size 640 x 520 pixels.
.SH QUICK START
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
#include <QApplication>
#include <Quarter/Quarter.h>
#include <Inventor/nodes/SoCone.h>
#include <Inventor/nodes/SoMaterial.h>
#include <Inventor/nodes/SoSeparator.h>
#include "QuarterExaminerViewer.h"

int main(int argc, char** argv)
{
    QApplication app(argc, argv);
    SIM::Coin3D::Quarter::Quarter::init();    // after QApplication

    SoSeparator* root = new SoSeparator;
    root\->ref();
    SoMaterial* mat = new SoMaterial;
    mat\->diffuseColor.setValue(1.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f);
    root\->addChild(mat);
    root\->addChild(new SoCone);               // no camera: the viewer adds one

    {
        QuarterExaminerViewer viewer;
        viewer.setSceneGraph(root);
        viewer.show();
        app.exec();
    }   // the viewer must be destroyed before Quarter::clean()

    root\->unref();
    SIM::Coin3D::Quarter::Quarter::clean();
    return 0;
}
.fi
.RE
.SS Building
.PP
The supplied \fBCMakeLists.txt\fR builds a static library
\fBquarterexaminerviewer\fR and the \fBhello_cone\fR test program. Link
your own targets against the library to inherit the include path and
the Qt, Coin, Quarter and OpenGL dependencies:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
target_link_libraries(myapp PRIVATE quarterexaminerviewer)
.fi
.RE
.PP
If Quarter and Coin are not found automatically, pass
\fB\-DQUARTER_ROOT=<prefix>\fR and \fB\-DCOIN_ROOT=<prefix>\fR, or the
directories containing their CMake config files. Set
\fB\-DQUARTER_QT_MAJOR=5\fR or \fB6\fR if Qt auto\-detection chooses a
version different from the one Quarter was built with.
.SH VIEWER DECORATION
.SS Buttons (left strip)
.TP 18
.B Pick
Pick mode: mouse events go to the scene graph (for manipulators,
selection, etc.). Arrow cursor.
.TP 18
.B View
View mode: the mouse navigates the camera. Hand cursor.
.TP 18
.B Home
Return to the stored home viewpoint.
.TP 18
.B Set Home
Store the current viewpoint as the home viewpoint.
.TP 18
.B View All
Fit the whole scene in the window.
.TP 18
.B Seek
Fly to an object: press, then left\-click the target.
.TP 18
.B Camera
Switch between perspective and orthographic camera. The icon shows the
type that a click switches to.
.SS Thumbwheels
.TP 18
.B Rotx
Left strip, bottom: Orbit the camera about its horizontal axis.
.TP 18
.B Roty
Bottom strip: Orbit the camera about its vertical axis.
.TP 18
.B Dolly
Right strip: Move the camera towards or away from the scene (or change
the view height for an orthographic camera).
.PP
All rotations are about the camera's focal point. The decoration can be
hidden with \fBsetDecoration(false)\fR or the popup menu.
.SH MOUSE AND KEYBOARD
.SS View mode
.TP 18
.B Left drag
Rotate (orbit about the focal point)
.TP 18
.B Middle drag
Pan
.TP 18
.B Ctrl + left drag
Pan
.TP 18
.B Ctrl + middle drag
Zoom
.TP 18
.B Shift + left drag
Zoom
.TP 18
.B Mouse wheel
Zoom (wheel up = closer)
.TP 18
.B Right click
Popup menu
.SS Keyboard
.TP 18
.B Esc
Toggle between Pick and View mode
.PP
In View mode the mouse belongs to the viewer: no mouse event, hover
included, is passed to the scene graph. In Pick mode the mouse events
are passed on to Quarter and the scene graph; only the right\-click
popup menu and the Esc key remain handled by the viewer. The mouse
cursor over the canvas is an open hand in View mode (closed while
dragging), an arrow in Pick mode and a crosshair while a seek is armed.
.SH POPUP MENU AND PREFERENCES
.SS Popup menu (right click)
.IP \(bu 3
\fBFunctions\fR: Home, Set Home, View All, Seek.
.IP \(bu 3
\fBViewing\fR: toggle View / Pick mode.
.IP \(bu 3
\fBDraw Style\fR: As is, Wireframe, Wireframe overlay, Hidden line,
Points, Bounding box.
.IP \(bu 3
\fBTransparency Type\fR: None, Screen door, Add, Delayed add, Sorted
object add, Blend, Delayed blend, Sorted object blend.
.IP \(bu 3
\fBOrthographic Camera\fR: toggle camera type.
.IP \(bu 3
\fBHeadlight\fR, \fBDecoration\fR: toggles.
.IP \(bu 3
\fBPreferences...\fR: opens the preferences dialog.
.SS Preferences dialog
.TP 18
.B Seek animation time
Duration of the seek flight in seconds (0 = jump immediately).
.TP 18
.B Seek distance
Percentage of the current camera\-to\-target distance kept after a seek
(default 50 %). For an orthographic camera this scales the view height.
.TP 18
.B Seek to
\fBPicked point\fR or \fBObject center\fR (center of the picked
object's bounding box).
.TP 18
.B Camera zoom
Field of view of a perspective camera in degrees (disabled for an
orthographic camera).
.TP 18
.B Background color
Opens a color chooser.
.TP 18
.B Transparency type
Quarter transparency mode.
.TP 18
.B Headlight
Enable or disable the headlight.
.PP
Changes take effect immediately; the dialog only has a Close button.
.SH ENUMERATIONS
.TP
.B enum CameraType { Perspective, Orthographic }
The camera projection. Used by \fBcameraType()\fR and
\fBsetCameraType()\fR.
.TP
.B enum DrawStyle { AsIs, Wireframe, WireframeOverlay, HiddenLine, Points, BoundingBox }
How the scene is rendered. Maps onto Quarter's render modes.
.TP
.B enum TransparencyType { NoTransparency, ScreenDoor, Add, DelayedAdd, SortedObjectAdd, Blend, DelayedBlend, SortedObjectBlend }
How transparent objects are rendered. Maps onto Quarter's transparency
types. \fBNoTransparency\fR ignores transparency (everything is drawn
opaque); \fBScreenDoor\fR uses stipple patterns and needs no sorting;
the \fBAdd\fR and \fBBlend\fR families use additive or alpha blending,
where the \fBDelayed\fR variants draw transparent objects after the
opaque ones and the \fBSortedObject\fR variants also sort the
transparent objects back to front. The initial value is whatever the
Quarter widget starts with; read it with \fBtransparencyType()\fR.
.SH PUBLIC FUNCTIONS
.SS Construction
.TP
.B explicit QuarterExaminerViewer(QWidget* parent = nullptr)
Creates the viewer: a \fBQuarterWidget\fR surrounded by the decoration.
Quarter must already have been initialized with \fBQuarter::init()\fR,
which in turn requires an existing \fBQApplication\fR.
.TP
.B ~QuarterExaminerViewer()
Detaches the scene graph from Quarter and releases the viewer's
references. The viewer must be destroyed before \fBQuarter::clean()\fR
is called.
.SS Scene graph and camera
.TP
.B void setSceneGraph(SoNode* scene)
Sets the scene to display. The viewer takes its own reference on
\fBscene\fR, so the caller keeps (and must eventually release) its own.
Any previous scene is released; passing \fBnullptr\fR clears the
viewer.
.IP
If the scene contains no \fBSoCamera\fR, the viewer creates an
\fBSoPerspectiveCamera\fR, places it ahead of the scene, fits it to the
scene when the window is first shown and stores that view as the home
position. If the scene already contains a camera, it is used unchanged
and its current state is stored as the home position.
.TP
.B SoNode* getSceneGraph() const
Returns the scene passed to \fBsetSceneGraph()\fR, or \fBnullptr\fR.
.TP
.B SoCamera* getCamera() const
Returns the camera in use (the viewer's own or the scene's), or
\fBnullptr\fR if no scene is set. Use it to apply changes to the camera
directly. The pointer changes when the camera type is switched, so do
not cache it across \fBsetCameraType()\fR / \fBtoggleCameraType()\fR;
connect to \fBcameraTypeChanged()\fR to be told when that happens.
After modifying the camera yourself, call \fBviewAll()\fR and/or
\fBsaveHomePosition()\fR as needed.
.TP
.B SIM::Coin3D::Quarter::QuarterWidget* quarterWidget() const
Returns the wrapped Quarter widget for functionality not exposed here.
.SS State queries
.TP
.B bool isViewing() const
True in View mode, false in Pick mode.
.TP
.B bool isHeadlight() const
True if the headlight is enabled.
.TP
.B bool isDecoration() const
True if the buttons and thumbwheels are shown.
.TP
.B CameraType cameraType() const
The current camera projection.
.TP
.B DrawStyle drawStyle() const
The current draw style.
.TP
.B TransparencyType transparencyType() const
The current transparency type. The value is read from the Quarter
widget, so it stays correct if the widget was changed directly through
\fBquarterWidget()\fR. If Quarter is set to a mode that has no
\fBTransparencyType\fR equivalent, the last value set through
\fBsetTransparencyType()\fR is returned.
.TP
.B QColor backgroundColor() const
The current background color.
.SS Seek settings and popup menu
.TP
.B void setSeekTime(double seconds)
Duration of the seek animation. 0 jumps immediately. Default 2.0.
.TP
.B double seekTime() const
Returns the seek time.
.TP
.B void setSeekDistance(float percent)
Percentage of the distance to the target that remains after a seek.
Default 50.
.TP
.B float seekDistance() const
Returns the seek distance.
.TP
.B void setSeekToObject(bool on)
If true, seek to the center of the picked object's bounding box instead
of the picked point. Default false.
.TP
.B bool isSeekToObject() const
Returns the seek target setting.
.TP
.B void setPopupMenuEnabled(bool on)
Enables or disables the right\-click popup menu.
.TP
.B bool isPopupMenuEnabled() const
Returns whether the popup menu is enabled.
.SH PUBLIC SLOTS
.TP
.B void viewAll()
Fits the whole scene in the window. Does nothing without a camera.
.TP
.B void saveHomePosition()
Stores the current camera position, orientation, focal distance and
view size as home.
.TP
.B void resetToHomePosition()
Restores the stored home viewpoint and cancels any seek animation.
.TP
.B void seek()
Arms seek: the next left click on the canvas picks a target and the
camera flies to it. A click on the background does nothing.
.TP
.B void setViewing(bool viewing)
Selects View mode (true) or Pick mode (false). Updates the buttons and
cursor and emits \fBviewingChanged()\fR.
.TP
.B void setHeadlight(bool on)
Enables or disables the headlight, which always shines along the
viewing direction.
.TP
.B void setDecoration(bool on)
Shows or hides the buttons and thumbwheels.
.TP
.B void setCameraType(CameraType type)
Switches the projection by replacing the camera node in the scene
graph, preserving position, orientation and apparent size. Emits
\fBcameraTypeChanged()\fR. Does nothing if the camera cannot be
replaced (for example if its parent is not a group node).
.TP
.B void toggleCameraType()
Switches between perspective and orthographic.
.TP
.B void setDrawStyle(DrawStyle style)
Sets the render style.
.TP
.B void setTransparencyType(TransparencyType type)
Sets how transparent objects are rendered. The change is applied to the
Quarter widget immediately and is reflected in the popup menu and the
preferences dialog. Use \fBBlend\fR for general use; use
\fBSortedObjectBlend\fR when overlapping transparent objects must look
correct from every direction, and \fBScreenDoor\fR when sorting is too
costly or alpha blending is not available.
.TP
.B void setBackgroundColor(const QColor& color)
Sets the background color.
.TP
.B void showPreferences()
Shows the modal preferences dialog.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B void viewingChanged(bool viewing)
Emitted when the Pick/View mode changes.
.TP
.B void cameraTypeChanged(QuarterExaminerViewer::CameraType type)
Emitted after the camera node has been replaced. Call \fBgetCamera()\fR
again to obtain the new camera.
.SH PROTECTED FUNCTIONS
.TP
.B bool eventFilter(QObject* obj, QEvent* ev) override
Filters events of the Quarter canvas to implement mouse navigation,
seek picking, the popup menu and the Esc key. Reimplement and call the
base implementation to add custom handling.
.TP
.B void showEvent(QShowEvent* ev) override
Performs the initial fit of a viewer\-created camera once the viewport
size is known.
.SH NOTES
.SS Lighting
.PP
The headlight is separate from the scene graph and always follows the
camera. A light node inside the scene (for example the
\fBSoDirectionalLight\fR in the Inventor Mentor "Hello, Cone" example)
is fixed in world space and therefore appears to turn with the object
when you orbit. Omit scene lights and use the headlight if you want the
light to follow the view.
.SS Camera ownership
.PP
A camera created by the viewer is part of the viewer's private root
node, not of your scene graph; your scene is not modified. A camera
that is part of your scene is used and modified in place.
.SS Lifetime
.PP
The viewer holds references on the scene and on its private root.
Destroy the viewer before calling \fBQuarter::clean()\fR, and release
your own scene reference after the viewer is gone or at any time after
\fBsetSceneGraph()\fR if you no longer need the scene.
.SS Differences from SoQtExaminerViewer
.IP \(bu 3
No spin animation after releasing a drag.
.IP \(bu 3
No stereo viewing, axes cross or help/set\-up\-view menu items.
.IP \(bu 3
Navigation is implemented by the viewer, not by Quarter's scxml
navigation systems; Quarter's own navigation is bypassed in View mode.
.IP \(bu 3
Draw styles and transparency types are those provided by Quarter.
